{"type": "spr", "stem": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A right circular cone has a height of <math alttext=\"22 centimeters left parenthesis cm right parenthesis\"><mrow><mn>22</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>centimeters</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mtext>cm</mtext></mfenced></math> and a base with a diameter of <math alttext=\"18 cm\"><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>cm</mtext></math>. The volume of this cone is <math alttext=\"n pi cm cubed\"><mi>n</mi><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>cm</mtext><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi>\n</math>?</p>", "keys": ["594"], "rationale": "<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"594\"><mn>594</mn></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the right circular cone has a height of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22 c m\"><mn>22</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and a base with a diameter of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"18 c m\"><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. Since the diameter of the base of the cone is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"18 c m\"><mn>18</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, the radius of the base is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9 c m\"><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The volume <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V\"><mi>V</mi></math>, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c m cubed\"><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, of a right circular cone can be found using the formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals one third pi r squared h\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#960;</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>h</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> is the height, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cm\"><mtext>cm</mtext></math>, of the cone and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> is the radius, in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"cm\"><mtext>cm</mtext></math>, of the base of the cone. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"22\"><mn>22</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h\"><mi>h</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math> in this formula yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals one third pi left parenthesis 9 right parenthesis squared left parenthesis 22 right parenthesis\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#960;</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>9</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>(</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"upper V equals 594 pi\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>594</mn><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#960;</mo></math>. Therefore, the volume of the cone is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"594 pi italic c m cubed\"><mn>594</mn><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#960;</mo><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the volume of the cone is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n pi italic c m cubed\"><mi>n</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#960;</mo><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"n\"><mi>n</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"594\"><mn>594</mn></math>.</p>", "externalid": "adc9a053-ace5-4475-8499-b52461f5f6e1", "correct_answer": ["594"]}